// Deploy: npm run build && npx wrangler pages deploy dist --project-name oryele-website
//
// ── KV (Newsletter subscribers) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. Cloudflare dashboard → KV → Create namespace → name: "oryele-subscribers"
// 2. Copy the namespace ID shown after creation
// 3. Paste it below replacing REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KV_NAMESPACE_ID
// 4. Pages → oryele-website → Settings → Functions → KV namespace bindings
//    Binding name: SUBSCRIBERS → select "oryele-subscribers"
//
// To view subscribers:
//   Cloudflare dashboard → KV → oryele-subscribers → View
//   Each key: subscriber:<email>  Value: {email, source, subscribedAt}
//
// To export all subscribers as CSV, run from terminal:
//   npx wrangler kv key list --namespace-id=<your-id> | \
//     npx wrangler kv key get --namespace-id=<your-id> --prefix=subscriber: > subscribers.json
//
// ── AI Chat (Mistral on AWS) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CF Function at /api/chat proxies to Mistral at 52.87.253.29:8001
// AWS Security Group sg-091d3bfdc02eb52ab: add all Cloudflare IPv4 CIDRs on port 8001
// Optional: add MISTRAL_API_KEY secret if your Mistral server requires auth
//
// ── Local dev ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// npx wrangler pages dev dist --port 4321
// KV is automatically mocked. Set MISTRAL_LOCAL=true in .dev.vars to hit localhost:8001
{
  "name": "oryele-website",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-01",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./dist",}
